"<strong>Magnitudes.</strong> Astronomers measure how bright a star looks with its apparent magnitude V. Smaller numbers are brighter, and a difference of {#} magnitudes is a factor of exactly {#} in brightness. The absolute magnitude M is the magnitude the star would have if it were {#} parsecs ({#} light years) away:",
